#original-page(612pt, 792pt, none)[
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72.024pt, 83.18pt, "system efficiency, a detailed thermal model is needed to calculate the energy consumption of the ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 110.78pt, "thermal management system. Trovò et al. [13] presented an experimentally validated thermal ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 138.38pt, "model of a 9 kW/27 kWh VRFB with a current of up to 400 A, which considers entropic heat from ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 165.98pt, "main reactions, irreversible heat from crossover side reactions, and hydraulic losses of the pumps. ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 193.58pt, "According to their results, the stack temperature can exceed 50 °C at the end of the long-duration ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 221.18pt, "high-current discharge period, which declares the necessity of a cooling system to prevent ion ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 248.81pt, "precipitation. Multiple cooling possibilities have been investigated and modeled in the scientific ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 276.41pt, "literature. Reynard et al. [14] described a concept in which the electrolyte is cooled using a heat ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 304.01pt, "exchanger, and the flow battery is combined with a thermally regenerative electrochemical cycle ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 331.61pt, "to further improve battery efficiency by 5-9%. Trovò et al. [15] suggested that maintaining a low ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 359.21pt, "flow rate continuously or periodically during standby periods can remarkably decrease the stack ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 386.81pt, "temperature, meanwhile keeping the self-discharge losses moderate. Industrial-scale VRFBs are ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 414.43pt, "often placed in containers that need to be considered in thermal modeling. Shu et al. [16] ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 442.03pt, "considered the container in their model of a 30 kW/130 kWh system and defined the inner air with ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 469.63pt, "an additional balance equation in the thermal network. The latter contains the transferred heat from ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 497.23pt, "the components and the auxiliary equipment. The authors stated that active cooling, utilizing fans, ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 524.83pt, "is necessary when the ambient temperature varies between 25 and 45 °C. In a later article, the ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 552.43pt, "authors proposed a hybrid active cooling strategy using an air conditioner (AC) and fans for a ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 580.06pt, "30 kW/240 kWh system, which is necessary in a hot summer environment with an insulated ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 607.66pt, "container and long operation times [17]. Wang et al. [18] proposed a room temperature model of ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 635.26pt, "a 5 kW/60 kWh VRFB with an AC system and a cooling strategy that can turn off the AC during ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 662.86pt, "charging, and keep a maximum room temperature at 25 °C during discharging to save up to 48% ")
]

// arXiv source page 6
#original-page(612pt, 792pt, none)[
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72.024pt, 83.18pt, "of energy used by the AC system, compared to a continuous maximum 30 °C room temperature ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 110.78pt, "operation. ")
  #line-at(107.42pt, 138.38pt, "A few models can be found in the literature regarding multistack configurations. In reality, ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 165.98pt, "stack resistances may differ due to production tolerances. Chen et al. [19] demonstrated in their ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 193.58pt, "study that the overall module charging capacity can be improved by arranging stacks with similar ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 221.18pt, "resistance in the same branch. The authors presented in a later paper [20] that the effects of ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 248.81pt, "transport delay can be minimized with proper pipe geometry and flow rate optimization in a ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 276.41pt, "multistack VRFB. Later, Chen et al. [21] presented a simplified thermal model for a 250 kW ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 304.01pt, "battery with 8 stacks. Their results showed that the temperature difference between the stacks is ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 331.61pt, "negligible. The authors also included electrode permeability variation in their research and ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 359.21pt, "demonstrated that stacks with similar electrode permeability should be arranged in the same branch ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 386.81pt, "to improve power and capacity [22]. ")
  #line-at(107.42pt, 414.43pt, "A specific desired power output is feasible with different configurations, depending on the ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 442.03pt, "ratio of discharging current, cell number, and stack number. The configurations influence system ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 469.63pt, "efficiency. Therefore, this paper aims to present a detailed thermal, electrochemical, and hydraulic ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 497.23pt, "model significantly further developed from [23], especially the thermal model and the thermal ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 524.83pt, "management system. The model is used to investigate system efficiency and thermal management ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 552.43pt, "losses as a function of power output, cell number, and discharging current. A lumped parameter ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 580.06pt, "model is presented with 14-27 nodes depending on the number of stacks, supplemented with a ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 607.66pt, "hybrid active thermal management system which contains openable control dampers, fans, AC, ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 635.26pt, "and electrolyte flushing. A total of 180 configurations are investigated in 10 cases, with power ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 662.86pt, "output from 4 kW to 400 kW. Each constant power case is investigated with 18 different cell ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 690.46pt, "numbers, limiting the maximal discharging current to 50-250 A. ")
]

