  #line-at(371.95pt, 442.03pt, "decreases, the Joule heat increases ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 469.63pt, "due to the increasing absolute value of the current, compensating for the decreasing stack voltage ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 497.23pt, "to maintain the constant discharging power. The increasing absolute value of the current slightly ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 524.83pt, "increases the heat generated by the main reaction entropy as well. Moreover, the volume flow rate ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 552.43pt, "also needs to be increased as the ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(226.97pt, 552.43pt, "SoC")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(247.01pt, 552.43pt, " decreases to maintain the constant output power. The volume ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 580.06pt, "flow rate also depends on the discharging current, whose absolute value increases during ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 607.66pt, "discharging, thereby further enhancing the cooling effect of the pumped-in electrolyte. The more ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 635.26pt, "significant decrement in cell voltage in high current configurations results in more pronounced ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 662.86pt, "changes in discharging current, thus in Joule heat, volume flow rate, and heat from main reaction ")
]

// arXiv source page 32
#original-page(612pt, 792pt, (image("graphics/page-32.png", width: 435.5pt), 80pt, 378pt))[
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72.024pt, 83.18pt, "entropy, compared to low current configurations. Considering the discharging period at night, ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 110.78pt, "when the container walls are cooler than the stack, thermal radiation enhances heat rejection. ")
  #line-at(108.02pt, 138.38pt, "A flow factor of 2 was used during charging and 5 during discharging to reduce the ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 165.98pt, "warming effect of pumped-in electrolyte during charging and to exploit the colder electrolyte in ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 193.58pt, "the tanks for cooling during discharging. The resulting volume flow rate range is hence wide for a ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 221.18pt, "single unit, which limits the selection of suitable devices; however, a two-stage pump system can ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 248.81pt, "also be a solution. The volume flow rate ranges from 0.6 to 30 m³/h, and the pump head varies ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 276.41pt, "between 0.2 and 15 m in the investigated configurations. It is clear that the pumped-in electrolyte ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 304.01pt, "has a dominant role in the temperature variation of the stack; therefore, a dynamically modulated ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 331.61pt, "flow factor could be an efficient solution for thermal management. ")
]

