  #line-at(72.024pt, 133.82pt, "4. Conclusions ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(107.42pt, 161.42pt, "This study presents a concentrated parameter model of a containerized vanadium redox ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 189.02pt, "flow battery, supplemented by the detailed models of the auxiliary equipment and thermal ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 216.62pt, "management system. A total of 180 different configurations were simulated to investigate system ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 244.25pt, "efficiency as the battery output power was scaled up from 4 to 400 kW in 10 cases, and the ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 271.85pt, "discharging current varied from 50 to 250 A in 18 steps. The same one-pump-per-stack layout, ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 299.45pt, "spatial arrangement, cell size, charge-discharge profile, ambient conditions, and power-to-capacity ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 326.93pt, "ratio were used during upscaling to improve comparability. Based on the results, the following ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 354.53pt, "conclusions were drawn. ")
  #line-at(107.42pt, 382.13pt, "At a fixed power output, the lower the discharging current, the higher the electrical ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 409.75pt, "efficiency due to the decrease in ohmic losses. The electric efficiency range is between 68% and ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 437.35pt, "89%, with the output power causing only minor differences within this range. ")
  #line-at(107.42pt, 464.95pt, "The system efficiency range is between 43 and 66%, and it is higher in low-current ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 492.55pt, "configurations. However, it also depends on the power output of the stack; the higher the stack ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 520.15pt, "power output, the higher the system efficiency. The maximum achieved system efficiency is 58–")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 547.75pt, "60% in low-power output configurations and 64–66% in high-power output configurations. ")
  #line-at(107.42pt, 575.38pt, "The most significant losses are caused by the thermal management system, ranging from ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 602.98pt, "7.5% to 17% in low power output configurations, especially at minimal and maximal discharging ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 630.58pt, "currents, followed by the inverter at 11–12%, and then the pumping losses at 2–6.5%. However, ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 658.18pt, "the thermal management losses are decreased to 6–14.2% in high power output configurations, ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 685.78pt, "and the pumping losses are also reduced to 1–2%. ")
]

